From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jukfiuune <108091130+jukfiuune@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:49:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] (halium) init.rc: do not start bpfloader

bpfloader (netbpfload) ships in the Tethering APEX. Inside the Halium
container it aborts, and the APEX declares the service with
reboot_on_failure, so starting it reboots the container seconds into
boot. Stock Halium never hit this because it shipped no Tethering APEX,
so exec_start found no bpfloader service. The APEX is needed for mobile
data on recent Qualcomm devices (nicmd and qms link against a library
inside it), so it is being restored in vendor/halium/config.

Halium runs no netd and no system_server, so nothing uses the BPF
programs bpfloader would load. bpf.progs_loaded is not waited on
anywhere else. Don't start it, as odsign is already not started.
---
 rootdir/init.rc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rootdir/init.rc b/rootdir/init.rc
index af6a41a..3eabfb1 100644
--- a/rootdir/init.rc
+++ b/rootdir/init.rc
@@ -1161,7 +1161,10 @@ on load-bpf-programs
     # NOTE: Still requires CAP_SYSLOG and sepolicy allow rules to read /proc/kallsyms
     write /proc/sys/kernel/kptr_restrict 1
 
-    exec_start bpfloader
+    # Halium: do not start bpfloader. It aborts inside the container, and the
+    # Tethering APEX declares it with reboot_on_failure, which would reboot
+    # the container. Nothing in Halium uses the programs it loads.
+    # exec_start bpfloader
 
     # Restore kallsyms protection after bpf programs have been loaded.
     write /proc/sys/kernel/kptr_restrict 2
-- 
2.55.0

